state sec145-action: "Civil Action (35 U.S.C. 145)" by office effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 35 U.S.C. 145; 37 CFR 90.3
{
  group appeal-group
  note "De novo civil action in E.D. Va. against the USPTO Director. Allows introduction of new evidence not in the record. Must be filed within 63 days of PTAB decision. If applicant loses, USPTO may recover its attorney fees."
  _ "District court orders allowance" -> allowance { authority cite 35 U.S.C. 145; MPEP 1216 }
  _ "District court affirms — abandoned" -> abandoned-no-reply by applicant {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.135
    effort 0.hours
  }
}

chance appeal-dismissed: "Appeal Dismissed (No Brief)" by office effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 41.37; MPEP 1215.04
{
  group appeal-group
  note "No appeal brief filed within the 37 CFR 41.37 period — appeal stands DISMISSED by operation of the rule (MPEP 1215.04 [R-01.2024]). Consequence splits on the record: applications having NO allowed claims are abandoned; where an allowed claim exists, the examiner cancels the rejected/withdrawn claims and issues the application on the allowed claim(s) (MPEP 1215.04, ¶ 12.209)."
  _ "No allowed claims — application abandoned" -> abandoned-no-reply p 0.8 {
    authority cite MPEP 1215.04; 37 CFR 1.135
    note "Per MPEP 1215.04: 'Applications having no allowed claims will be abandoned.' Claims allowable only for their dependency from rejected claims are treated as rejected. Modeled at 0.8 (most appealed applications reach the Board with all claims under rejection)."
  }
  _ "Allowed claim(s) exist — examiner cancels rejected claims and issues" -> patent-issued p 0.2 {
    authority cite MPEP 1215.04 (¶ 12.209); 37 CFR 1.311
    note "Per MPEP 1215.04: where an allowed claim exists, the examiner cancels the nonallowed claims and allows the application on the allowed claim(s) — a salvaged (narrowed) patent rather than abandonment. Modeled at 0.2. Sum with the abandonment branch = 1.0."
  }
}

// `/// imported` keeps this declaration's unresolvable legacy citation a
// warning: its cite hole carries the original text, and cite-resolves
// checks hole reasons like cites (see the bead report). MPEP §§ 803,
// 818 and 2210-2214 are not vendored in sources/mpep.txt.
/// imported
decision restriction-requirement: "Restriction / Election Requirement" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite ?("37 CFR 1.142; 35 U.S.C. 121; MPEP 803") {
  group examination-group
  note "Examiner finds two or more independent and distinct inventions claimed in one application and requires restriction to one (37 CFR 1.142; 35 U.S.C. 121). Applicant must elect one invention for prosecution — with or without traverse (37 CFR 1.143). Non-elected claims are withdrawn from consideration; they may be pursued in a divisional application."
  elect-without-traverse "Elect invention WITHOUT traverse" -> election-made {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.142; 37 CFR 1.143; MPEP 818.01
    effort 3.hours
    within election-reply {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "37 CFR 1.136(a)"
      note "Election without traverse concedes the restriction; non-elected claims withdrawn. No petition right preserved."
    }
    duration { min 9.days, mode 30.days, max 60.days }
  }
  elect-with-traverse "Elect invention WITH traverse (preserve 37 CFR 1.144 petition)" -> election-made {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.143; 37 CFR 1.144; MPEP 818.01(d)
    effort 5.hours
    within election-reply {
      extendable true
      extension_authority "37 CFR 1.136(a)"
      note "Traverse preserves the right to petition the restriction requirement to the Director under 37 CFR 1.144 after a final requirement. Applicant must still elect and prosecute one invention."
    }
    duration { min 9.days, mode 30.days, max 60.days }
  }
}

// `/// imported` keeps this declaration's unresolvable legacy citation a
// warning: its cite hole carries the original text, and cite-resolves
// checks hole reasons like cites (see the bead report). MPEP §§ 803,
// 818 and 2210-2214 are not vendored in sources/mpep.txt.
/// imported
state election-made: "Election Filed" by examiner effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite ?("37 CFR 1.143; 37 CFR 1.144; MPEP 818") {
  group examination-group
  note "Applicant elects one invention. Election WITH traverse (37 CFR 1.143) preserves the right to petition the restriction requirement under 37 CFR 1.144 (petition to the Director, within the reply period); election WITHOUT traverse concedes it. Withdrawn (non-elected) claims may be prosecuted in a divisional under 35 U.S.C. 121."
  _ "Examiner examines elected claims — issues Office Action" -> non-final-oa {
    authority cite 35 U.S.C. 132; 37 CFR 1.104; MPEP 821.04
  }
  _ "File divisional for non-elected invention (35 U.S.C. 121 shield)" -> divisional-filed by applicant {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.53(b); 35 U.S.C. 121; MPEP 201.06
    effort 30.hours
    cost 2_000.usd
    note "Same filing/search/examination fees as an original nonprovisional: $2,000.00 undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025 ($350.00 + $770.00 + $880.00, 37 CFR 1.16(a)/(k)/(o))."
  }
}

state divisional-filed: "Divisional Application Filed" by office effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.53(b); 35 U.S.C. 121; MPEP 201.06
{
  group filing-group
  note "Divisional filed for the non-elected invention. 35 U.S.C. 121 SHIELD: a patent issuing on a divisional filed as a result of a restriction requirement (and complying with 35 U.S.C. 120) shall NOT be used as a double-patenting reference against the other application/patent (35 U.S.C. 121, 3rd sentence; MPEP 804.01). Divisional gets its own examination."
  _ "Divisional docketed — enters examination" -> pre-examination {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.104; MPEP 704
  }
}

state continuation-filed: "Continuation Application Filed" by office effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.53(b); 35 U.S.C. 120; MPEP 201.07
{
  group filing-group
  note "Continuation filed under 37 CFR 1.53(b) to pursue further claims to the same disclosure (MPEP 201.07). Must be co-pending — filed before the parent issues or goes abandoned. Claims the benefit of the parent's filing date under 35 U.S.C. 120. A common alternative to RCE/appeal that keeps the parent's prosecution posture alive in a fresh child."
  _ "Continuation docketed — enters examination" -> pre-examination {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.104; MPEP 704
  }
}

state advisory-action: "Advisory Action" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.116; MPEP 714.13; MPEP 706.07(f)
{
  group after-final-group
  note "Examiner issues an Advisory Action responding to an after-final amendment (typically not entering it, or entering it for appeal purposes only). CRITICAL: filing the after-final amendment does NOT toll the running of the statutory period for reply to the final rejection — 'The filing of an amendment after final rejection, whether or not it is entered, does not stop the running of the statutory period for reply' (MPEP 714.13). The 35 U.S.C. 133 six-month clock keeps running from the final rejection date; extensions may still be needed to preserve the appeal/RCE window."
  _ "Advisory Action received — reassess (clock still running, MPEP 714.13)" -> after-final-decision {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.116; MPEP 714.13
    effort 1.hours
    note "The 1.116 filing bought no time — applicant must still appeal, file an RCE/continuation, or otherwise reply before the 6-month 35 U.S.C. 133 ceiling, taking 37 CFR 1.136(a) extensions as needed."
  }
}

state noa-received: "Notice of Allowance Received" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.311(a); MPEP 1306
{
  group allowance-group
  note "Notice of Allowance specifies the issue fee and any required publication fee. Both are due 3 months from the NOA mailing date. This period is NOT extendable — 37 CFR 1.311(a); MPEP 1306 [R-01.2024]: 'The period for payment of the issue fee and any required publication fee is not extendable, see 37 CFR 1.311(a).' No extension of time under 37 CFR 1.136(a) or (b) is available. Trap: unlike a shortened statutory period for reply, there is NO safety-valve extension here — miss the 3 months and the application is abandoned; only a 37 CFR 1.137 revival petition (unintentional delay) can restore it."
  _ "Pay issue fee within 3 months" -> issue-fee-paid {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.311(a); 37 CFR 1.18(a); MPEP 1306
    effort 1.hours
    cost 1_290.usd
    within issue-fee {
      extendable false
      note "Issue fee due 3 months from NOA. NOT extendable under any authority — 37 CFR 1.311(a); MPEP 1306 [R-01.2024]. No 37 CFR 1.136(a)/(b) extension is available. Late payment = abandonment; only a 37 CFR 1.137 revival petition (unintentional delay) can restore the application."
    }
    duration { min 13.5.days, mode 45.days, max 90.days }
    valence good
    note "Utility issue fee $1,290.00, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025 (37 CFR 1.18(a)(1))."
  }
  _ "Fail to pay issue fee — abandonment" -> abandoned-issue-fee {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.311; 37 CFR 1.135
    effort 0.hours
    valence bad
  }
}

state issue-fee-paid: "Issue Fee Paid" by office effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.311; 37 CFR 1.18; MPEP 1306
{
  group allowance-group
  note "Issue fee and publication fee (if required) paid. Application forwarded for patent printing. Applicant may file a continuation, divisional, or CIP before the patent issues to pursue additional claims."
  _ "Patent issues" -> patent-issued { authority cite 35 U.S.C. 151; MPEP 1309 }
}

terminal patent-issued: "Patent Issued" by applicant outcome [win, issued] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 35 U.S.C. 151; MPEP 1309
{
  group allowance-group
  note "Patent granted. 20-year term from nonprovisional filing date (35 U.S.C. 154(a)(2)), subject to patent term adjustment (PTA) for USPTO delays and patent term extension (PTE) for regulatory review under 35 U.S.C. 156. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $1,000,000, override per matter, matching this project's full-win stake convention."
  valence good
  payoff 1_000_000.usd
  _ "Maintenance fees become due (3.5 / 7.5 / 11.5 years)" -> maintenance-due {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.362; 35 U.S.C. 41(b)
    effort 0.2.hours
  }
  _ "Third party challenges the issued patent (post-grant)" -> patent-challenged by office {
    authority cite 35 U.S.C. 311; 321; 302
    note "The post-grant afterlife. Modeled as a world event off the (terminal) issuance node — like the existing patent-issued→maintenance-due edge, this out-edge is walked by the simulator but treated as absorbing by the from-start EV/absorbing-chain analysis (issuance is a terminal). The adversarial sub-chain rooted here is analyzed on its own — see design/graph-algorithms.md §8.5."
  }
  reissue-narrowing-filed "File narrowing reissue application (§ 251; any time during enforceable term)" -> reissue-pending {
    authority cite 35 U.S.C. § 251; 37 CFR 1.171; MPEP 1401
    effort 20.hours
    cost 3_670.usd
    note "Narrowing reissue may be filed at any time during the enforceable term. Only spec/claims/drawings needed for filing date; oath may follow (37 CFR 1.53(f); MPEP 1403). Original patent surrendered on filing, remains in force during prosecution (§ 252). Reissue filing fees $3,670.00 total, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025: $350.00 basic filing (37 CFR 1.16(e)) + $770.00 search (1.16(n)) + $2,550.00 examination (1.16(r)) -- the reissue examination fee is well above the $880.00 utility examination fee."
  }
  reissue-broadening-filed "File broadening reissue application — MUST be within 2 years of grant (§ 251)" -> reissue-pending {
    authority cite ?("35 U.S.C. § 251, ¶ 4; MPEP 1412")
    effort 25.hours
    cost 3_670.usd
    within broadening-reissue {
      extendable false
      note "Two-year broadening window from the date of patent grant. Filing on the anniversary date is timely (MPEP 1403). After it closes, broadening reissue is gone FOREVER — an unextendable, irreversible forfeiture (flag mpep/broadening-window-closed)."
    }
    duration { min 109.5.days, mode 365.days, max 730.days }
    valence good
    note "Reissue filing fees $3,670.00 total, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025: $350.00 basic filing (37 CFR 1.16(e)) + $770.00 search (1.16(n)) + $2,550.00 examination (1.16(r)) -- the reissue examination fee is well above the $880.00 utility examination fee."
  }
  _ "Miss 2-year broadening reissue window — broadening permanently barred" -> patent-issued {
    authority cite ?("35 U.S.C. § 251, ¶ 4; MPEP 1412")
    effort 0.hours
    valence bad
    note "The 2-year broadening window closes. Flag mpep/broadening-window-closed raised. Narrowing reissue remains available; broadening does not."
  }
}

state maintenance-due: "Maintenance Fees Required" by applicant effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.362; 35 U.S.C. 41(b)
{
  group allowance-group
  note "Maintenance fees required at 3.5, 7.5, and 11.5 years after grant (37 CFR 1.362). A 6-month grace period with surcharge is available. Failure to pay within the grace period = expiration. Small and micro entities pay reduced fees."
  _ "Pay maintenance fee on time" -> maintenance-due {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.362; 37 CFR 1.20(e)-(g)
    effort 0.5.hours
    cost 2_150.usd
    valence good
    note "3.5-year maintenance fee $2,150.00, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025 (37 CFR 1.20(e)); the 7.5-year fee is $4,040.00 (1.20(f)) and the 11.5-year fee is $8,280.00 (1.20(g)) -- this edge's self-loop models only the recurring 3.5-year-tier default since the pack has no windowed-maintenance-cycle state."
  }
  _ "Fail to pay maintenance fee — patent expires" -> patent-expired {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.362(f); 35 U.S.C. 41(b)
    effort 0.hours
    valence bad
  }
}

terminal abandoned-no-reply: "ABANDONED — Failure to Reply" by applicant outcome [loss, abandoned, waiver-trap] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 35 U.S.C. 133; 37 CFR 1.135
{
  group examination-group
  note "PERMADEATH. Application abandoned for failure to reply within the 6-month statutory ceiling. The 6-month period under 35 U.S.C. 133 cannot be extended for any reason. Revival requires a petition under 37 CFR 1.137 (unintentional delay standard). Revival is not guaranteed. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $0, override per matter."
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
  _ "Petition to revive — unintentional delay (37 CFR 1.137)" -> applicant-response-window {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.137; 37 CFR 1.17(m); MPEP 711.03(c)
    effort 4.hours
    cost 2_260.usd
    note "Revival requires (1) the required reply, (2) the petition fee under 37 CFR 1.17(m), and (3) a statement that the ENTIRE delay from the due date until the reply was UNINTENTIONAL (37 CFR 1.137(a)). Revival is not guaranteed and does not undo intervening rights. Reinstates the open reply window. Petition fee $2,260.00, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025, for delay of 1 year or less (37 CFR 1.17(m)(2)); a delay exceeding 1 year is $3,000.00 (1.17(m)(1))."
  }
}

terminal abandoned-issue-fee: "ABANDONED — Issue Fee Not Paid" by applicant outcome [loss, abandoned, waiver-trap] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.311; 37 CFR 1.135
{
  group allowance-group
  note "PERMADEATH. Application abandoned for failure to pay the issue fee within the extended period. Revival available under 37 CFR 1.137 for unintentional delay. Competitor may have relied on abandonment — revival does not undo intervening rights. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $0, override per matter."
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
  _ "Petition to revive — pay issue fee late (37 CFR 1.137)" -> noa-received {
    authority cite 37 CFR 1.137; 37 CFR 1.17(m); MPEP 711.03(c)
    effort 4.hours
    cost 2_260.usd
    note "Same 37 CFR 1.137 unintentional-delay standard + 37 CFR 1.17(m) petition fee. Because the issue-fee period is itself unextendable (MPEP 1306), revival is the ONLY route back after a missed issue fee. Reinstates the allowance posture so the issue fee can be paid. Petition fee $2,260.00, undiscounted/large-entity, effective 1/19/2025, for delay of 1 year or less (37 CFR 1.17(m)(2)); a delay exceeding 1 year is $3,000.00 (1.17(m)(1))."
  }
}

terminal patent-expired: "Patent Expired" outcome [loss, expired, waiver-trap] effective [2024-01-31, ..) cite 37 CFR 1.362; 35 U.S.C. 41(b)
{
  group allowance-group
  note "Patent expired for failure to pay maintenance fees after the 6-month grace period. Reinstatement is not available for expired patents (unlike abandoned applications). The invention enters the public domain. PLACEHOLDER PAYOFF: $0, override per matter. Premature expiration for a missed maintenance-fee payment, not the natural end of a full term."
  valence bad
  payoff 0.usd
}
